    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21485" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illātĕnus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illactĕnus</span></b> , adv.
		illetenus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>so far</i> (post-class. and very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">navitas precum ejus (Arionis) commiseritum esse
					illactenus, ut, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 16, 19, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">litteras illatenus, qua dixi, legendas
					praebebat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Mag. p. 326</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Fronto Ter. Als. 4</span></i>.</div>
